8.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {25 and 74}

The double-sestina rotation of the six terminal words is preserved exactly in every stanza of the supplied text; therefore the only admissible swap is between two lines that terminate on the identical word. Lines 25 and 74 are the sole such pair (both end on “music”).  

Exchanging them restores the canonical opening of the fifth Strephon stanza (“Long since … music / Hath made itself …”) and supplies the expected three-line envoi coda, while every other stanza and the rotation rule remain untouched. All rival suggestions either exchange lines with mismatched end-words (thereby breaking multiple stanzas) or leave the attested syntactic fracture at 25-26 unrepaired.

